Z||000000||Marc Harris||11-23-2001||11:53 PM||||Swapping out the IAC eliminated my code 35 problem and my 87 4cyl passed the smog test this morning.  The car's been sitting for almost 5 years and hasn't had a smog check since '96 but it passed with no problem.<P>The car runs like new when warm but when cold it still doesn't maintain a steady idle. I was hoping the IAC would solve that problem but no such luck. Now there are no codes so I'm going to have to find the problem the hard way. <P>Marc Harris<BR>San Jose, CA||||reg||1
Z||000001||clayatandalusia||11-24-2001||01:04 AM||||Check out your TPS on the Back of the rodchester TBI i think it has two T-15 bolts holding in in if it is stock.. you'll have to remove the TBI to get to them .. or  i always have so not to have damaged heads on my origonal screws... be careful on your wires you can get the connector confused with the MAP sensor ... The MAP is a Green Connector i think ... Happy troubleshooting<P>Clay<BR>||||reg||3
